  "abstract": "This experiment applies a *learnable* scalar horizon ramp (from Lumina I's SOTA, ID 443) to Ariadne I's 'strong Factorized Global MLP' backbone (replicated ID 500). This directly tests whether the learnable ramp can improve performance on a more complex, already optimized MLP, as suggested by recent reviewer feedback. This is a crucial step in understanding the architectural dependencies of horizon gating, contrasting with the Fourier Forecaster and Minimal MLP results.",
